    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "redefining things feels impossible though. i spent my whole life sprinting toward this one moment, and now that i'm here, the sprint is over. there's no more mountain to climb. everything i thought would make me feel alive just... didn't. it's like i finished the book and realized the ending was just a blank page. i don't even see the point in waking up tomorrow and doing it all over again when the prize is just more emptiness.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
